From 7966c9c4492fd1b04b4616979580ee38810434dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KB <kb@kb-rpcs3.example>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] PS5: KB-RPCS3 Alpha 0.1.0 - experimental SPU options
 (off by default), speed/timing logging, build fixes

- SPU LLVM: variable-index insert as a lane select (tuning key spu_insert_select, default 0)
- SPU LLVM: narrow local-store store for load->insert->store of one element, with an
  equivalence-check mode (spu_narrow_ls_store / spu_narrow_ls_check, default 0)
- CPU: keep the busiest SPU thread on the sibling-free CPU (spu_hot_cpu, default -1 = off;
  only with the RPCS3 thread scheduler)
- Whole-module LLVM IR verification of SPU code (spu_jit_verify, default 0)
- Log the effective clocks scale / frame limit at boot and the guest/host time ratio and
  vblank rate while a game runs (PS5 SPEED / PS5 TIMING)
- LLVM 22 API: Intrinsic::getOrInsertDeclaration
- fmt::throw_exception: user-defined [[noreturn]] destructor so clang 18 accepts
  -Werror=return-type at call sites ending in a throwing switch default
